{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/lem-su2-emergence-dagger-unitarity","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Lemma","doco:Section"],"label":"lem:su2-emergence-dagger-unitarity","kind":"lemma","title":"Inner-product-preserving $2 \\times 2$ matrices lie in $\\mathrm{U}(2)$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-fiber-adjoint-involution","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-positive-definite-dagger"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-su2-emergence-dagger-unitarity"],"tags":["frobenius","dagger","unitarity","u2"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.su2_emergence_dagger_unitarity","text":"su2-emergence-dagger-unitarity.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"lem:su2-emergence-dagger-unitarity\"></a><p>Identify <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tau(V)</code> with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{C}^2</code> and its Frobenius dagger structure with the standard Hermitian inner product <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\langle x, y \\rangle = \\bar{x}^{\\mathsf T} y</code>. If a <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2 \\times 2</code> complex matrix <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">g</code> satisfies <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\langle g x, g y \\rangle = \\langle x, y \\rangle</code> for all <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">x, y \\in \\mathbb{C}^2</code>, then <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">g \\in \\mathrm{U}(2)</code>. Consequently, any set <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">G</code> of such matrices satisfies <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">G \\subseteq \\mathrm{U}(2)</code>.</p>\n<p>The identification itself (that the dagger structure on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tau(V)</code> is a positive-definite Hermitian form, that <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\dim \\tau(V) = 2</code>, and that every tensor automorphism preserves it) is a hypothesis of this statement, not a conclusion.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/su2-emergence-dagger-unitarity.md","heading":"Lemma","number":"4.2.7","page":"b/lem-su2-emergence-dagger-unitarity","qa":{"counts":{"pass":92,"fail":1,"warn":2,"na":24,"unknown":0,"stale":94},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":1}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.StandardModel.su2_emergence_dagger_unitarity","via":"ref","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/su2_emergence_dagger_unitarity.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
